{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":4808343,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,16]],"date-time":"2026-08-16T04:13:57Z","timestamp":1786853637090,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":22,"publisher":"IOP Publishing","issue":"24","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,18]],"date-time":"2016-05-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1463529600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/publishingsupport.iopscience.iop.org\/iop-standard\/v1"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,18]],"date-time":"2016-05-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1463529600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"funder":[{"name":"European Metrology Research Programme"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2016,6,22]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Strain characterization by transmission electron microscopy is an active area of research especially for microelectronics applications. Two-wave dark-field electron holography (DFEH) was previously introduced as a reliable strain mapping technique. Here, DFEH with four electron waves was investigated in order to image equi-displacement lines as amplitude modulations of the holographic fringes. Two perpendicular electrostatic biprisms are used to interfere three reference waves diffracted by a substrate and one object wave diffracted by an epitaxially strained region. This technique provides a different way to represent the displacement field. It might be helpful to obtain information about the strain state during\n                    <jats:italic>in situ<\/jats:italic>\n                    experiments. A dummy\n                    <jats:italic>p<\/jats:italic>\n                    -MOSFET device with embedded SiGe source and drain is used for experimental demonstration.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1088\/0022-3727\/49\/24\/244003","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,18]],"date-time":"2016-05-18T12:13:31Z","timestamp":1463573611000},"page":"244003","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":7,"title":["Four-wave dark-field electron holography for imaging strain fields"],"prefix":"10.1088","volume":"49","author":[{"given":"T","family":"Denneulin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"CEMES"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"M","family":"H\u00fftch","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"CEMES"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"266","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"daa20fdbib001","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1086","DOI":"10.1038\/nature07049","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Nanoscale holographic interferometry for strain measurements in electronic devices","volume":"453","author":"H\u00fftch","year":"2008","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"daa20fdbib002","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1584","DOI":"10.1007\/s11664-011-1623-z","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Mobility enhancement technology for scaling of CMOS devices: overview and status","volume":"40","author":"Song","year":"2011","journal-title":"J. Electron. Mater."},{"key":"daa20fdbib003","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0268-1242\/26\/12\/125010","type":"journal-article","article-title":"The reduction of the substitutional C content in annealed Si\/SiGeC superlattices studied by dark-field electron holography","volume":"26","author":"Denneulin","year":"2011","journal-title":"Semicond. Sci. Technol."},{"key":"daa20fdbib004","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.3358149","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Strain evolution du